{"id":161778557966914,"type":"album","name":"American Gothic","artist":"David Ackles","year":1972,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://dn721909.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-e8515590-3cf2-46a5-9855-a4a608f87883/mbid-e8515590-3cf2-46a5-9855-a4a608f87883-23134350829.png","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"sS0bP7qAxsY","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/6w4b41IacQMT1aFAldWRrh","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_m4YDjVOcVOFbfWccSs79jSrZTm57aHO14","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/david-ackles/american-gothic"},"desc":"The years have only been kind to the album considered David Ackles' masterpiece when it was released. Ackles combined an early-'70s singer/songwriter sensibility with a theater music background that placed him as much in the tradition of Brecht-Weill and Jacques Brel as Bob Dylan. Not only are his songs fully realized, dramatic statements, but Ackles proves himself a warm, accomplished singer. When this album got no higher than #167 in the charts, Ackles' fans were heartbroken. Decades later, American Gothic remains one of those great albums that never found its audience. It waits to be rediscovered. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":211028922511213,"name":"David Ackles","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/2251bf55c9bc090237f450f03ff464ed/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":163536058891268,"type":"genre","name":"Traditional Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":211,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":135407159101775,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Traditional Pop","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":185,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":65232636722211,"name":"Scaruffi 1970s","src":"charts",